pacing=\"3pt\"><mtr><mtd><munder><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">lim</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>4</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>0</mn><mn>0</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<p>So, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"24\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mtable style=\"min-width: 18.98em;\"><mjx-table><mjx-itable><mjx-mtr><mjx-mtd style=\"text-align: right; padding-right: 0.139em; padding-bottom: 0.5em;\"><mjx-munder><mjx-row><mjx-base style=\"padding-left: 0.262em;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6C\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c69\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-base></mjx-row><mjx-row><mjx-under style=\"padding-top: 0.167em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2192\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msup><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.289em;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx